return "PNDR-0770 is a humanoid equipped with psychic abilities of mind-control and reality distortion; powers of which are potent enough to cause severe deterioration of its corporeal form. Though it seldom resorts to physical violence, it is primarily a psychological agent of destruction; its default method of warfare is to destroy targets’ minds and rewire them to kill as many victims as possible. Cunning as it is erratic, its ultimate stated goal is to rewrite the laws of physics as it sees fit. PNDR-0770 is a male humanoid of standing height 175.2 cm and absolute zero mass. Its skin is colored a deep navy blue and emits a neon blue outline measuring 2.1 mm thick. Cysts of the outline’s same color grow along its torso, left arm, and part of its left leg. Its skeleton has fused with its skin – bones of which protrude out its integumentary system and are also colored a dark blue. It employs steel robotic eyes, heart, plugs along its shoulder pads and spine, joints, and jaws. Its corporeal form appears somewhat frail and sickly; it also moves with stiff, robotic mannerisms though shows no complications from any physical impairment. No organism or organic matter can physically interact with PNDR-0770; biological substances phase through its body as if it were not there. PNDR-0770’s corporeal form is not restricted to reality’s boundaries. It can \"phase\" between physical substantialness and insubstantialness at will. When phased out, PNDR-0770 cannot be seen and holds no physical bearing upon space. However, its presence can still be detected through a deep, drawing noise that emanates from anywhere it probes. Communication usually involves telepathy, where human subjects report hallucinating subliminal messages and hearing noises such as tones, whispers, and a man’s laughter while being hunted by PNDR-0770. It may also use electronic means of contact via email or SMS text messaging. All text written by PNDR-0770 appears in all-caps. Emails it sends always originate from an address of arbitrary UTF-8 symbols ranging from 1-20 characters long each for usernames and domains. Text messages to mobile phones always appear from random and often fictional area codes for numbers. While in this state, it will patrol an area of expanding radius for humans to target. Once a target is acquired, it will move towards them and phase in once close enough. A target will know if he is being pursued by PNDR-0770 through the groaning noise becoming louder and deeper. When phasing in, it releases a flash of blue light distorting the visual perception of its surroundings and leaving behind a blue, shadowy silhouette indicating its position when entering reality. Noises of loud buzzing and/or children laughing often accompany this phenomenon. Similar effects often occur when phasing out, though they seem to only exist in the human mind, as cameras and audio recording devices do not detect them occurring outside humans’ perception, though they do capture PNDR-0770 itself manifesting. Once ready, it then runs toward and attacks any nearby human. PNDR-0770 will phase back out any time it fails to catch a target or sustains enough physical trauma to kill multiple people, healing itself of some damage each time. However, while PNDR-0770 does heal much faster than humans, it does not heal immediately; it can suffer enough physical damage to become physically incapacitated, not even being able to phase out, allowing for containment. Reducing PNDR-0770 to this state is taxing on time and resources, given its repertoire of ways to elude P.N.D.R. Company offensive forces. As PNDR-0770 is physically insubstantial against biological entities, it cannot inflict direct bodily harm upon humans. Instead, it uses non-physical means of destroying victims’ minds and assuming control over their bodies. Being within 1.5 meters of PNDR-0770 causes swift cognitive decline in humans, onsetting symptoms such as auditory and visual hallucinations, delusions, motor control failure, seizures, and dissociation within ten (10) seconds. Symptoms intensify until the victim is suddenly rendered catatonic, at which point PNDR-0770 attempts a remote takeover of their brain, overwriting their consciousness. In 85% of all brain takeover attempts, the victim then quickly starts to seep from their eyes, mouth, and nose a black liquid consistent with PNDR-0770's blood with their skin paling and hair slowly turning white. At this point, they are formally declared an instance of PNDR-0770-2. Subentities are extremely violent, relentlessly moving to kill the nearest target until neutralized via lethal force. PNDR-0770-2 experiences constant transient hypertrophy across their body, creating muscle tension and nutrient delivery allowing for elevated physical strength and endurance. If an incapacitated target does not fully succumb to PNDR-0770 after 1-2 minutes, though, they will reawaken with symptoms of amnesia and confusion that subside after up to twelve (12) hours. Survivors report seeing PNDR-0770 while in a dream-like state promising to let them live if they complete a game of his, which often involves escaping labyrinthine structures or choosing the correct one of a series of identical-looking paths. Although sociable, PNDR-0770 employs a defiant and erratic personality – not only does it habitually disobey orders from authority, but it continually concocts ways to defy the constraints of reality while phased in. It is so fixated on breaching boundaries, that it has proclaimed to one day find a way to redefine the laws of physics as it sees fit (appendix to be added). It has published mathematical papers challenging -the legitimacy of all knowledge regarding physics and exposing the universe’s \"spatial malleability\". Peer reviewers have critiqued its proofs for their rambling and at-times incomprehensible ideas and language. Its papers’ anomalous implications also make replication among institutions outside the P.N.D.R. Company impossible. Demonstrations of PNDR-0770’s ideas remain within the confines of STATION: ██ under strict supervision and restrictions (see Containment Guidelines). Recent studies suggest a growing ability to manipulate not just human minds, but physical space itself within an exponentially expanding radius, posing questions about the future security of its containment facility."